{"archetypes":[{"name":"ship-resume","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Large Python ship driver resume changes span PR identity, CI counters, OOS gating, merge, and postmerge behavior.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new Python ship resume state machine and how it interacts with existing fresh, open PR, merged, forked, draft, repo-unavailable, and gh-skipped flows. Trace whether persisted counters, PR identity, branch identity, OOS state, and postmerge state are hydrated and rewritten consistently across all early returns and stalled paths. Pay special attention to off-by-one loop limits, skipped final-report comments on resume, and behavior when gh or git validation fails. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"state-hygiene","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Persisted ship state is newly parsed and rewritten, making validation and containment mistakes high impact.","prompt_body":"Review the persisted ship state handling as untrusted input, including state_file containment, branch and repo validation, PR URL validation, merge-result validation, conflict file CSV validation, and newline injection checks. Check whether any invalid state can steer checkout assumptions, PR operations, shell-readable state output, or conflict-handoff metadata unsafely. Consider stale or partially corrupt state files and whether fallbacks are fail-closed where identity matters. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pause-restore","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The design pause restore primitive and marker lifecycle changed in ways sensitive to shell error handling and retry semantics.","prompt_body":"Inspect the design pause loader's replacement of git archive with guarded git ls-tree enumeration and per-file git show extraction. Verify the implementation is safe under set -euo pipefail, preserves structured LOAD_OK and ERROR output on ls-tree or show failures, recreates nested files correctly, and does not accidentally treat extraction failures as missing artifacts. Check that marker deletion happens only after successful install and that marker-delete failures remain non-fatal while being surfaced. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"route-contract","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The new MARKER_CLEARED and WARN behavior must stay consistent across loader, router, skill prompt, docs, and tests.","prompt_body":"Trace the pause-load output contract through design-route.sh, the design skill prompt, result-env allowlists, docs, and regression assertions. Verify MARKER_CLEARED, WARN, ERROR, LOAD_OK, and resume step values are parsed, deduplicated, emitted, and persisted consistently without dropping loader diagnostics on success or failure paths. Check cancel-pause-load and LOAD_OK=false fallthrough behavior for stale marker and failed delete cases. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sentinel-publish","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The publisher now accepts non-step .completed sentinels and must avoid widening the staging surface unexpectedly.","prompt_body":"Review the design-log publish change that allows emit_plan, tally, finalize, and validate_plan_commands under .completed alongside step-* sentinels. Confirm the allowlist exactly matches design-driver normalized action names and that every other unexpected basename still fails with the intended diagnostic. Check whether docs and structure tests would catch future allowlist drift or accidental acceptance of broader filenames. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-realism","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff relies heavily on shell and Python regression harness changes with complex stubs and real-git reproductions.","prompt_body":"Examine whether the updated shell and Python tests faithfully exercise the new behavior rather than only the stubs. For the pause-resume harness, check the git and gh stubs, failure injection knobs, stub-free real-git export-ignore reproduction, cwd binding, and marker-retention assertions. For the Python tests, check that resume counters, durable flags, PR recovery, CI monitor persistence, and postmerge resume cases cover realistic command outputs and failure modes. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
